These SVG files are Codicons, Visual Studio Code's icon set.

    Source:    https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-codicons
    Copyright: (c) Microsoft Corporation
    License:   CC BY 4.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Fetched from src/icons/ in that repository, unmodified on disk. The
activitybar package substitutes the documents' fill="currentColor" for a
concrete colour before rasterizing, which is a render-time substitution
and not a change to these files.

browser.svg and window.svg are byte-identical, and that is upstream's
doing rather than a bad copy here: Codicons ships `browser` as an alias
of `window`, and both src/icons/ files hash to
f2ed5124abc7b6231c7fd47a4f516369. Both names are kept because a catalog
name IS a filename here. TestShippedIconsAreDistinctAssets hashes this
directory and carries that pair as its one recorded allowance, so a
genuinely mis-copied glyph still reddens.

VERIFIED 2026-08-30: every file here was fetched from src/icons/ on that
repository's main branch and compared byte for byte. All 33 match. The
recipe is in components/activitybar/icons/LICENSE, which carries the
same claim for its five; running it there without running it here would
verify the smaller half.

CC BY 4.0 permits use and modification, commercial included, and requires
attribution — which is what this file is. Keep it beside the icons.
